{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review disposition: fixed the required-site blocker by explicitly adding all seven existing workflow parsing/lint/policy tests to the plan and recorded file impact, preserving their legacy-continuity assertions while retargeting them to the thin wrappers. Also fixed the shallow-clone ambiguity with exact exit 2/stderr and fixed repair-pause ownership with per-invocation repair:<surface>:<uuid4> tokens, foreign-pause abort semantics, and operator-only recovery (no automatic retry reclaim). Accepted the GitLab pin advisory because immutable URL + committed provenance + checksum/dialect verification fail closed at retrieval. Accepted the remaining P6/scope advisories: the multi-provider matrix is intentionally one atomic portability contract sharing one entrypoint/constants table; splitting it would permit provider drift, while each observable is individually enumerated in the ACs."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786299053099280001,"uuid":"627e4abb-ea5c-4c73-9d09-a8c13224f656"}